  "production_and_recognition_observations": [
    "269 replaces freely classifying and stating each q with evaluating coupled classification/q claims. In particular, rejecting C alone can use its first ratio 2!=4 rather than independently proving non-geometric status; the reviewer still verified its full ratios 2,4,4,4,2.",
    "270 does not establish that the learner independently wrote all five terms. In (a)-(d), the second term already distinguishes all four options. This is mathematical recurrence-based elimination, not a copied answer, but the reduced calculation demand must not be described as five independent computations.",
    "270(e) and 270(f) deliberately have two candidates sharing the correct first two terms; a third-term radical multiplication is necessary to distinguish them. Recognizing a whole tuple still does not prove independent calculation of every later entry.",
    "271 replaces written ratio and term calculation with paired-result recognition. Each item has another option with the right q but the wrong term, so q alone cannot select the correct option.",
    "272 tests inverse recurrence and prefix order, not free written recovery or a written proof that both later ratios agree.",
    "273 tests recognition of formulas, nonuniqueness, and feasibility, not free derivation of the formulas.",
    "274 tests recognition of all feasible tuples or real nonexistence, not free written construction or proof.",
    "275 tests classification and named constants directly from recurrences, not independent prose explanations or general-term derivation.",
    "276 cannot certify construction of examples not already supplied or a general monotonicity proof. It retains recognition of all four cases and the sign-dependent direction. Its E/F distractors satisfy their numerical conditions and fail only their direction claims.",
    "277 tests exact interval/set recognition, not independent written inequalities, intersection work, and endpoint justification."
  ],
